{"id": "met-438389", "status": "ok", "meta": "Madame Reiset, mother of the Louvre curator Frédéric Reiset, painted by Anne-Louis Girodet in 1823.", "about": "Colette-Désirée-Thérèse Godefroy, who lived from 1782 to 1850, was the wife of Jacques de Reiset, a French government official of the Restoration era. She was the mother of Frédéric Reiset, the art collector and curator at the Louvre. Anne-Louis Girodet painted her portrait in 1823. It is now in the Metropolitan Museum of Art in New York.", "museum_record": "https://www.metmuseum.org/art/collection/search/438389", "inventory_number": "1999.101", "dimensions": "23 3/4 x 19 1/2 in. (60.3 x 49.5 cm)", "credit_line": "Purchase, Gifts of Joanne Toor Cummings, Mr. and Mrs. Richard Rodgers, Raymonde Paul, and Estate of Dorothy Lichtensteiger, by exchange, 1999", "sources": ["https://www.metmuseum.org/art/collection/search/438389", "https://collectionapi.metmuseum.org/public/collection/v1/objects/438389", "https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q19912314", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Portrait_of_Madame_Reiset"], "check": "clean"}
