{"id": "getty-e6bc2dbc-e781-41b6-912a-6e361cefd6fd", "status": "ok", "meta": "An unkempt alchemist weighs a substance among his clutter in Cornelis Bega's small panel of 1663.", "about": "The unkempt alchemist sits among a chaotic jumble of equipment, unaware of the mess around him. He holds a scale and weighs a substance for one of his experiments in making gold. The Getty notes that by the seventeenth century alchemy was no longer thought a respectable science. Cornelis Bega painted the small oil panel in 1663.", "museum_record": "https://www.getty.edu/art/collection/object/103RFX", "inventory_number": "", "dimensions": "", "credit_line": "", "sources": ["https://www.getty.edu/art/collection/object/103RFX"], "check": "clean"}
