{"id": "si-saam_1972.151.1", "status": "ok", "meta": "A young man with rosy cheeks and long whiskers in his best clothes, painted by William Page in the 1830s.", "about": "William Page was at the height of his career when he painted this portrait. By 1834 he was fully established in the New York art world as a member of the American Academy, and a year later he was on its board. That left him no shortage of wealthy patrons. He shows this genteel sitter in his finest clothes, with rosy cheeks and lips framed by fashionably long whiskers.", "museum_record": "https://americanart.si.edu/collections/search/artwork/?id=19173", "inventory_number": "", "dimensions": "", "credit_line": "", "sources": ["https://americanart.si.edu/collections/search/artwork/?id=19173"], "check": "clean"}
