{"id": "cma-151807", "status": "ok", "meta": "Paris gives the golden apple to Venus in Joachim Wtewael's Judgment of Paris, painted in 1602.", "about": "The Trojan prince Paris was asked to decide which goddess was the most beautiful. Hera, at the left of the group, offered him political power, and Athena, seen from the back, offered military skill. Paris gave the golden apple to Venus, goddess of love, who promised him Helen, the most beautiful mortal in the world. Joachim Wtewael painted the scene in 1602.", "museum_record": "https://clevelandart.org/art/1984.14", "inventory_number": "1984.14", "dimensions": "", "credit_line": "Mr. and Mrs. William H. Marlatt Fund", "sources": ["https://clevelandart.org/art/1984.14", "https://openaccess-api.clevelandart.org/api/artworks/151807"], "check": "clean"}
